<title>SOUTH KOREA: Strikes cost S.Korea 2.6 trln won in lost output.</title>
<headline>Strikes cost S.Korea 2.6 trln won in lost output.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-01-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea is expected to post 2.6 trillion won in lost production by the end of Friday due to labour strikes disrupting major industries, a trade ministry statement said.</p>
<p>Lost exports from the start of industrial action on December 26 were estimated to be $467 million, it said.  </p>
<p>The strikes are in protest against the passage of a new labour law, which allows employers to lay off workers, replace strikers and implement flexible work hours.</p>
<p>--Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5644</p>
</text>
